# PKDB-Bench: factual_lookup instance
# In what year did each current EU member state join the European Union?
#
# Wikidata model:
#   ?country -- P463 (member of) --> Q458 (European Union)
#   The qualifier pq:P580 on the P463 statement records the start time
#   (accession date). pq:P582 records end time; absence means the
#   membership is still active.
#
# Universe filter: include only current members (no P582 end-time
# qualifier). This excludes the UK (P582 = 2020-01-31, post-Brexit).
#
# Per the SPARQL gotchas guide (references/sparql-gotchas.md §1 Option B):
# - This query needs the statement-node form (p: / ps: / pq:) because we
#   read qualifiers (P580 start time, P582 end time). The truthy `wdt:P463`
#   shortcut cannot expose qualifiers.
# - Rank handling: the statement-node form would otherwise pick up
#   deprecated-rank statements too. We exclude deprecated rank explicitly
#   via FILTER NOT EXISTS on wikibase:DeprecatedRank to use the safer
#   "preferred + normal rank" subset. The result is the same 27 current
#   members either way (verified by audit), but excluding deprecated
#   rank explicitly is the documented safer default.
# - Universe filter: P582 end-time absence excludes Brexit-departed UK
#   (UK's P463=Q458 statement has P582 = 2020-01-31).
SELECT ?countryLabel (YEAR(?startDate) AS ?accessionYear) WHERE {
  ?country p:P463 ?statement .
  ?statement ps:P463 wd:Q458 .                                    # member of European Union
  ?statement pq:P580 ?startDate .                                 # accession (start time)
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?statement pq:P582 ?endDate . }             # current member only
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?statement wikibase:rank wikibase:DeprecatedRank . }  # exclude deprecated rank
  SERVICE wikibase:label { bd:serviceParam wikibase:language "en". }
}
ORDER BY ?accessionYear ?countryLabel
